        <h2>Summary / Description</h2>
        <div class="description">
          Dataset represents the HARV biofilm growth and microscopy in the form of graphs and orthoganol CLSM images. Detailed data descriptions can be found below and included with each figure legend. Treatment details follow the dataset description.
<p>
Figure 1: CFU/ml of S. mutans hydroxyapatite (HA)-grown biofilms (left; n=3 independent experiments) and microcarrier bead biofilms (right; n=2 independent experiments). Cells from S. mutans BM cultures grown for 16 hours in HARVs (microgravity and normal gravity conditions, 35 RPM each) were harvested by low-speed centrifugation, and CFU/ml were determined for both the HA-associated biofilms (pellet) and planktonic bacteria (supernatant). Error bars = SEM. *Student 2-tailed t-test (p = 0.083).
<p>
Figure 2: Representative confocal microscopy of S. mutans microcarrier beadgrown biofilms. Microcarrier bead biofilms from S. mutans BM cultures (n=2 independent experiments) grown for 16 hours in HARVs (microgravity and normal gravity conditions, 35 RPM each) were harvested by low-speed centrifugation, and biofilms were transferred to optically-clear 96-well plates and z-stack images were acquired at 400x magnification. Representative orthoganol views are shown. Green= GFP-expressing S. mutans.
<p>
Figure 3: Representative confocal microscopy of S. mutans-S. gordonii microcarrier bead-grown biofilms. Microcarrier bead biofilms from S. mutans BM cultures (n=2 independent experiments) grown for 16 hours in HARVs (microgravity and normal gravity conditions, 35 RPM each) were harvested by low-speed centrifugation, and biofilms were transferred to optically-clear 96-well plates and z-stack images were acquired at 400x magnification. Representative orthoganol views are shown. Red = RFPexpressing S. gordonii, Green = GFP-expressing S. mutans.
<p>
For each experiment, overnight S. mutans cultures were used to inoculate sterile BM containing 11 mM glucose and 10 mM sucrose to an OD600 = 0.06. Each inoculum was supplemented with 0.5 mg/ml hydroxyapatite (HA) powder (Sigma) or microcarrier beads prior to growth for 16 hours at 35 RPM. HARV (10-ml size) cultures were then transferred to 50-ml Falcon tubes, and centrifuged at 1000 RPM for 10 minutes. Culture supernatants were transferred to a new tube, and HA or bead-associated cells (pellet) were resuspended in 2 ml sterile HBSS by vigorous pipetting and vortexing. CFU/ml for each of the culture supernatant and biofilm (pellet) fractions was determined by serial dilution plating. For confocal laser scanning microscopy, S. mutans cultures expressing GFP and/or S. gordonii cultures expressing RFP were inoculated (each to final OD600 = 0.03), grown, and biofilms harvested as described above, and carefully transferred to an optically-clear flat bottom 96-well plate. z-stack images were acquired by CLSM (400X magnification).
        </div>

